# End-to-End Feature Creation Guide

> When adding a complete feature, create files in this order to avoid gaps.
> Examples below use **Feature** as a representative module — adapt names to your actual feature.

## Standard Steps

### 1. Type Definitions

\`\`\`ts
// src/types/feature.ts
export interface FeatureItem {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  // ...actual project fields
}

export interface FeatureListParams {
  page: number;
  pageSize: number;
}
\`\`\`

### 2. API Functions

\`\`\`ts
// src/api/feature.ts
import type { FeatureItem, FeatureListParams } from "@/types/feature";


export const fetchFeatureList = (params: FeatureListParams) => {
  return fetch(\`/api/features?page=\${params.page}\`);
};
\`\`\`

### 3. Reusable Hook (Optional)

\`\`\`ts
// src/hooks/useFeature.ts
export function useFeature(id: string) {
  // Encapsulate data fetching, loading state, and error handling
  // Components call this directly; don't duplicate fetch logic
}
\`\`\`

### 4. Page Component

\`\`\`tsx
// src/components/FeatureList/FeatureList.tsx
// Rendering only; business logic lives in Hook / Store
export function FeatureList() {
  // 1. Get data from store/hook
  // 2. Handle loading / error states
  // 3. Render the list
}
\`\`\`

### 5. Route Registration

\`\`\`tsx
// src/routes/index.tsx or route config file
{ path: "/features", element: <FeatureList /> }
{ path: "/features/:id", element: <FeatureDetail /> }
\`\`\`

## File Checklist

After adding a feature, confirm the following files were created/updated:

- [ ] \`src/types/feature.ts\` — Type definitions
- [ ] \`src/api/feature.ts\` — API functions
- [ ] \`src/hooks/useFeature.ts\` — Data hook (optional)
- [ ] \`src/components/FeatureList/\` — Page component
- [ ] Route config updated

---

*Follow this pattern for project consistency. See @project-structure.mdc for actual directory locations.*
