    "content": "---
description: How to call backend APIs: file location, client usage, error handling
alwaysApply: false
globs: src/api/**
---


# API Call Guidelines

## Core Conventions

- Keep all API functions in \`src/api/\`, split by business module
- **Do not** call \`fetch\`/\`axios.get\` directly in components/stores — use wrapper functions
- Each function does one thing: request + return data (handle side effects at the call site)

## HTTP Client

> ⚠️ Could not auto-detect the project's HTTP client wrapper. Check the project's API request wrapper and ensure calls go through wrapper functions.

## Do / Don't

\`\`\`ts
// ❌ Direct fetch in component
useEffect(() => {
  axios.get("/api/features").then(setList);
}, []);

// ✅ Call wrapper function
useEffect(() => {
  fetchClientList({ page: 1, pageSize: 20 }).then(setList);
}, []);
\`\`\`

## Error Handling

Each API function must handle exceptions, or the caller must try-catch. 

