# Project Structure

See also: @global-rules.mdc

## 📁 Directory Tree

Main project directory structure:

\`\`\`text
└── src/ # source code
    ├── api/ # API definitions
    ├── pages/ # pages
    ├── store/ # state management
    └── utils/ # utilities
\`\`\`


## 📋 Directory Purpose Reference

Detailed purpose for important directories, including file types and naming conventions:

> 💡 See @code-style.mdc for naming conventions and code style

### \`src/api/\`

**Purpose**: API definitions

- Sample files: \`client.ts\`

### \`src/pages/\`

**Purpose**: pages — 1 files — component

- Sample files: \`Home.tsx\`

### \`src/store/\`

**Purpose**: state management

- Sample files: \`useUserStore.ts\`

### \`src/utils/\`

**Purpose**: utilities

- Sample files: \`safeFetch.ts\`


## 🎯 File Organization (Quick Reference)

Common file type locations for quick lookup:

### Utilities

**Location**: \`src/utils/\`

**Organization**: Group by concern (e.g. \`date.ts\`, \`validation.ts\`)

### API

**Location**: \`src/api/\`


## ✨ New File Guidelines

### File Location Decision Table

> When creating a new file, use this table to find the correct directory; if unsure, follow a similar existing file.

| File type | Location | Example filename |
|-----------|----------|------------------|
| Page / reusable component | \`src/pages/\` | \`UserList.tsx\` |
| Utility function | \`src/utils/\` | \`format.ts\`, \`validate.ts\` |
| API / Service | \`src/api/\` | \`user.api.ts\` |




---
*Before creating new files, see this file for correct directory locations and naming conventions.*
